The only example I can think of which is even remotely similar is the
David Eddings serieses (Belgariad, and you don't need to read any
others). In those, magic can be used for any purpose except to destroy
an object. (The gods who created the world are displeased with the
idea of someone undoing their work.)

But there's no ethical component there. You can tear a human being to
shreds, or hit him with lightning, or create a ten-ton boulder over
his head and watch the result. You just can't annihilate mass.

